--TEST--
A `foreach` over a `Core\ObjectSet`, `Core\ObjectMap` or `Core\Heap` walks what the collection held when the loop began, so the body may add to it, remove from it or clear it, and both sides are named: what the loop reached and what the collection holds afterwards, pinning `rule:iteration/foreach-subjects`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:iteration/core-collections-are-iterable
// Each block asserts the bound from both directions. The first number is what
// the loop reached, which is what the collection held at the `foreach`; the
// second is what it holds after the body's changes. A collection that walked
// live instead would fail the first, and one that discarded the body's
// changes would fail the second.

// A set the body adds to on every round.
var $tags = new Core\ObjectSet<int>();
$tags->add(1);
$tags->add(2);
$tags->add(3);
var $walked = "";
foreach ($tags as int $tag) {
    $walked = $walked . $tag . ";";
    $tags->add($tag + 10);
}
echo $walked, " ", $tags->count(), "\n";

// A map the body empties on its first round. The walk still reaches all three
// keys, and the map is empty when it ends.
var $stock = new Core\ObjectMap<string, int>();
$stock->set("a", 1);
$stock->set("b", 2);
$stock->set("c", 3);
int $keys = 0;
foreach ($stock as string $name) {
    $keys = $keys + 1;
    $stock->clear();
}
echo $keys, " ", $stock->count(), "\n";

// A heap the loop does not empty. Two walks in a row give the same elements in
// the same order, and the heap still holds every one of them.
var $costs = new Core\Heap<int>();
$costs->push(30);
$costs->push(5);
$costs->push(17);
var $once = "";
foreach ($costs as int $cost) {
    $once = $once . $cost . ";";
}
var $twice = "";
foreach ($costs as int $cost) {
    $twice = $twice . $cost . ";";
}
echo $once == $twice ? "same" : "different", " ", $once, " ", $costs->count(), "\n";

// `pop` is the member that removes one, and it answers what both walks
// reached first.
echo $costs->pop(), " ", $costs->count(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
1;2;3; 6
3 0
same 5;17;30; 3
5 2
